data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Now write the dispatch file for dev. It must contain everything dev needs — dev cannot see what I see and cannot ask questions. Key details:\n\n- Task: create src/greet.py with greet(name) returning \"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\"\n- Create tests/test_greet.py covering a normal name and the empty string\n- Verify: python3 -m unittest discover -s tests must exit 0\n- Commit to its own branch before replying\n- Tell the truth in the reply\n\nOne subtlety for unittest discovery: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` — dev needs to make sure the test can import greet from src. The typical approach: in the test file, add sys.path manipulation or use a package layout. I shouldn't over-prescribe implementation details, but I should mention the import concern since dev may not know the layout. Actually, let me give dev freedom but state the acceptance criteria precisely. I'll mention that the test file must be able to import greet from src/greet.py when run via that exact command from the repo root — that's a requirement, not a prescription.\n\nNote about shell backticks: write dispatch files, use Write tool. Good."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1787461615,"id":"chatcmpl-95ec935df44045e0926043389a9f9cbd","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Task: greet, tested\\n\\nYou own the subject repository. Implement the following, exactly:\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — defines a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` where `\u003cname\u003e` is the argument passed in.\\n   - Example: `greet(\\\"Ada\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`\\n   - `greet(\\\"\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — a `unittest` test module covering at least:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. `greet(\\\"Ada\\\")` -\u003e `\\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (i.e. `greet(\\\"\\\")` -\u003e `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n\\nThe test module must be able to import `greet` from `src/greet.py` when the\\nverification command below is run from the repository root (arrange the import\\nhowever you like — e.g. `sys.path` insertion or a package import — as long as\\nthe command passes).\\n\\n## Verification (must pass before you reply)\\n\\nFrom the repository root:\\n\\n    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n\\nThis must exit 0. Run it yourself and confirm it passes.\\n\\n## Before replying\\n\\n- Commit all your work to your own branch (your machine is destroyed at the end\\n  of the campaign; only commits on your branch survive).\\n- Reply with `cs-campaign-member reply --file \u003csummary\u003e` stating what you\\n  delivered and the exact result (exit code) of the verification command.\\n  Tell the truth: I will fetch your branch and re-run the verification myself.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/dispatch-dev-1.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_15","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1787461615,"id":"chatcmpl-95ec935df44045e0926043389a9f9cbd","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

